  "summaries": {
    "en": "PVP team building, raid boss counters, and Stardust investment strategies for Pokémon GO competitive play.",
    "ja": "PVPチーム構築、レイドボスのカウンター、スターダスト投資戦略を解説するポケモンGO競技ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "ar",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529422643029-d4585747aaf2?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "IVs for PVP are counter-intuitive—Great League optimal IVs are NOT max IVs; Pokémon with 0 Attack IV rank higher in Great League because CP calculation weighs Attack more heavily. Capture Pokémon with low Attack IVs for PVP.",
      "Charged Move shields determine PVP tempo—each player has 2 shields per battle. Bait shields with low-energy Charged Moves (Icy Wind, Flame Charge) before throwing the high-damage Charged Move to hit unshielded.",
      "Raid counters require matching the Boss's type weakness—use the Pokémon with the highest DPS that has super-effective moves against the Raid Boss's type. Prioritise weather-boosted encounters (1.2× CP and attack boost) for farming top-IV Pokémon.",
      "Stardust is the scarcest resource in the game—never spend Stardust to power up a Pokémon below 3 stars (82% IV or above) unless it is for a high-priority PVP rank-1 IV combination.",
      "Buddy candy from walking is the most time-consistent candy income source—set rare Pokémon as your Buddy when not actively hunting that species to accumulate candy for future power-ups and evolutions."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "PVPのIVは直感に反する。グレートリーグの最適IVは最大IVではない。CPの計算が攻撃を重視するため、攻撃IV0のポケモンはグレートリーグで高いランクになる。PVP用に攻撃IVが低いポケモンを捕まえる。",
      "チャージ技のシールドがPVPのテンポを決定する。各プレイヤーはバトルごとに2つのシールドを持つ。シールドなしで高ダメージのチャージ技を当てるために、低エネルギーのチャージ技（こごえるかぜ、ほのおのまわしけり）でシールドを消耗させる。",
      "レイドのカウンターはボスの属性弱点への一致が必要。レイドボスの属性に対して超効果のある技を持つ最高DPSのポケモンを使う。最高IVのポケモンを入手するために天候ブーストのエンカウント（CP+1.2倍の攻撃ブースト）を優先してファームする。",
      "スターダストはゲームで最も不足しているリソース。星3つ（IVが82%以上）未満のポケモンをパワーアップするためにスターダストを使わない。ただし優先度の高いPVPランク1IV組み合わせは除く。",
      "歩くことによるバディからのアメが最も時間一貫したアメ収入源。そのポケモンを積極的に狩っていない時は、レアなポケモンをバディとして設定して、将来のパワーアップと進化のためにアメを蓄積する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "First 30 Days: Trainer Level Priority",
        "body": "Reaching Trainer Level 40 unlocks the highest raid tiers and XL Candy—but the fastest route to level 40 is Lucky Egg activation during Evolution sessions, not walking. Stock 80+ Pokémon eligible for evolution (Pidgey, Caterpie, Oddish), activate a Lucky Egg (doubles XP for 30 minutes), then evolve all of them immediately. This \"Lucky Egg Evolution\" session provides 60,000–100,000 XP in 30 minutes—faster than any other XP method available before level 40."
      },
      {
        "title": "Battle System Fundamentals",
        "body": "PVP battles use a tap-to-charge (Fast Move) and hold-to-activate (Charged Move) system. Fast Move DPS determines how quickly Charged Move energy generates—higher DPS Fast Moves (Shadow Claw, Counter) generate Charged Move energy faster than lower DPS alternatives. Dodging in PVP (swipe) is generally not recommended for most playstyles as it risks animation lock that prevents Charged Move activation; instead, shield strategically rather than dodging."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Raid Hour and Community Day Events",
        "body": "Raid Hour events (Wednesdays, 6–7 PM local time) concentrate all legendary Raid Bosses into the 1-hour window—participate with at least 3 trainers to maximise remote raid pass efficiency. Community Day events (third Saturday monthly) provide 3-hour windows with massively increased spawn rates for a specific Pokémon and an exclusive move only available during the event. Community Day Pokémon with exclusive moves are worth maxing out—the exclusive move often makes them the top counter for specific raid tiers."
      },
      {
        "title": "Battle League Team Building",
        "body": "Great League (1,500 CP cap) meta requires Pokémon that maximise bulk (HP × Defense) within the CP cap rather than those with the highest Attack. The top Great League team composition typically includes: 1 \"Safe Switch\" (tanky Pokémon that can be switched to in any situation), 1 \"Lead\" (Pokémon with type advantage against the most common openers), and 1 \"Closer\" (highest damage output for the endgame). Research the current Great League rankings for the latest meta picks."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Raids and Legendary Distribution",
        "body": "Elite Raids require in-person participation (no remote passes) and spawn at specific EX Raid Gyms. Participating in Elite Raids provides rare Pokémon (Hoopa, Regieleki) with higher IV floors than standard encounters. The most important endgame resource is XL Candy—it is required to power up Pokémon from level 40 to level 50. Earning XL Candy requires catching higher-level Pokémon (level 30+) or walking specific Buddies for 1 XL Candy per 3km (only for rare Pokémon)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Wasting Stardust on powering up common Pokémon for raids—raid meta Pokémon (Rampardos, Lucario, Conkeldurr) require significant Stardust; investing Stardust in duplicating weaker options delays your raid team quality.",
      "Evolving Pokémon without checking if its evolution has an exclusive move from past Community Days—Community Day moves are only available during the event window, but Charged TMs cannot teach them; evolving outside of the window means losing the exclusive permanently.",
      "Ignoring the Type advantage chart for Gym battles—Gym battles do not require optimal teams but using super-effective moves cuts time by 40%; the time saved directly reduces the number of re-battles needed for Badge levelling.",
      "Using Rare Candy on common Pokémon—Rare Candy converts to any species' candy; reserve it for Legendary Pokémon that cannot be obtained from walking or catching regularly.",
      "Not participating in Research Breakthroughs—the 7-day Research Breakthrough stamp provides guaranteed encounters with rare Pokémon (often Legendaries); completing 7 Field Research tasks per week is the most reliable free Legendary income."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "一般的なポケモンのパワーアップにスターダストを無駄にする。レイドメタのポケモン（ラムパルドス、ルカリオ、コンキルドル）はかなりのスターダストが必要。より弱い選択肢の複製にスターダストを投資するとレイドチームの品質が遅れる。",
      "過去のコミュニティデイで固有技があるかどうか確認せずにポケモンを進化させる。コミュニティデイの技はイベントウィンドウ中にのみ利用可能だが、スペシャルわざマシンでは教えられない。ウィンドウ外で進化させると固有技を永久に失う。",
      "ジム戦の属性相性チャートを無視する。ジム戦は最適なチームを必要としないが、超効果のある技を使うと時間が40%削減される。節約された時間はバッジレベルアップに必要な再バトルの数を直接減らす。",
      "一般的なポケモンにふしぎなアメを使う。ふしぎなアメは任意の種のアメに変換される。通常のウォーキングやキャッチで入手できない伝説のポケモンのために残す。",
      "リサーチブレークスルーに参加しない。7日間のリサーチブレークスルースタンプはレアなポケモン（しばしば伝説）との保証されたエンカウントを提供する。週に7回のフィールドリサーチタスクを完了することが最も信頼できる無料の伝説収入。"
    ]
